        "original_id": "95975a6a-6161-5fa4-8d8e-662d11cc5d79",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Rhodochiton, Platystemon, Lophospermum\n- Taxonomy: Plantaginaceae, poppy family, monotypic genus, species naming\n- Places: southern Mexico, Guatemala\n\nFacts:\n- Rhodochiton is a genus of flowering plants in the family Plantaginaceae that is native to southern Mexico and neighbouring Guatemala.\n- Platystemon is a monotypic genus of flowering plants in the poppy family that contains the single species Platystemon californicus.\n- Platystemon californicus is known by the common name creamcups.\n- Lophospermum has a close relationship with other genera, particularly Maurandya and Rhodochiton.\n- The close relationship among Lophospermum, Maurandya, and Rhodochiton has caused confusion over the names of some species.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "cceb14ed-7dfe-5cdd-83b1-9641dc312005",
        "text": "Page: Rhodochiton. Sentence: Rhodochiton is a genus of flowering plants within the family Plantaginaceae, native to southern Mexico and neighbouring Guatemala.\nPage: Platystemon. Sentence: Platystemon is a monotypic genus of flowering plants in the poppy family containing the single species Platystemon californicus, which is known by the common name creamcups.\nPage: Lophospermum. Sentence: The close relationship with some other genera, particularly \"Maurandya\" and \"Rhodochiton\", has led to confusion over the names of some species.",
